IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing) Regulations (Rg 1, 2004 Revised Edition, 29.2.2004; G.N. No. S 21/80, amended to S 212/99), made under s 66 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-television-and-radio-licensing-regulations/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-RG1.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- THIS MODULE HOLDS THE TEXT AS THE REVISED EDITION 2004 PRINTS IT ("version 1"). S 333/2004 amended it from 21 June 2004 and S 548/2012 revoked it, deemed from 1 January 2011:
-- those are in `sgba-i-s333-2004.l4` and `sgba-i-s548-2012.l4`, and `sgba-versions.l4` says which text is read for which pair of days. Every function here is date-free.
-- Function names say what they are: "(RevEd 2004)" marks the text as printed in the Revised Edition; a regulation that S 333/2004 left alone is not repeated in the other module.
-- The Regulations say "broadcast matter transmitted by radio waves, wire or cable"; the Act's definition of "broadcasting apparatus" says "broadcasting service". Fork F-BA-10 (NOTES.md): the receiving facts are taken as the same facts.
-- No text of these Regulations before the Revised Edition of 29 February 2004 was obtained: the history line lists S 21/80, 46/83, 52/83, 314/83, 151/87, 105/88, 404/90, 125/91, 525/93, 87/95, 214/95, 291/96, 212/99, of which only S 212/99 was fetched (sgba-i-s212-1999.l4).

§ `The version row: the Revised Edition 2004`

-- src:32 | REVISED EDITION 2004
-- src:33 | (29.2.2004)
@ref the Revised Edition 2004 of the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations, dated 29.2.2004 (src:32-33)
-- Two dates, as for every version: it takes effect on the Revised Edition's date, and its date of publication is taken as the same day, because the PDF prints no separate publication line (the e-Gazette's Revised Subsidiary Legislation of 2004).
`Rg 1 as printed in the Revised Edition 2004` MEANS
    `Rg 1 version` WITH `source` IS "Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004 (29.2.2004), e-Gazette"
                      , `the text read` IS "RevEd 2004"
                      , `takes effect on` IS (Date 29 2 2004)
                      , `published on` IS (Date 29 2 2004)
                      , `the Regulations are in force` IS TRUE

§ `Regulation 2: Definitions`

-- src:139 | 2. —(1) In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise
-- src:140 | requires —
-- src:141 | ‘‘broadcast sound receiver’’ means any apparatus used for the
-- src:142 | aural reception of broadcast matter transmitted by radio
-- src:143 | waves, wire or cable;
-- src:144 | ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’ means any apparatus used for
-- src:145 | the aural reception, and the visual reception in monochrome
-- src:146 | or colour, of broadcast matter transmitted by radio waves,
-- src:147 | wire or cable but does not include any Television Receive-
-- src:148 | Only Satellite Receiving System;
-- src:149 | ‘‘hotel’’ means any premises registered under the Hotels Act
-- src:150 | (Cap. 127) for use as a hotel;
-- src:151 | ‘‘Television Receive-Only Satellite Receiving System’’ or
-- src:152 | ‘‘TVRO system’’ means any apparatus (including a dish
-- src:153 | antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of
-- src:154 | direct reception of broadcast matter emitted from or passing
-- src:155 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in
-- src:156 | extra-terrestrial space;
@ref reg 2(1) "broadcast sound receiver", "broadcast television receiver", "hotel", "TVRO system" (RevEd 2004) (src:139-156)
GIVEN a IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the apparatus is a broadcast sound receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    a's `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`

GIVEN a IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the apparatus is a TVRO system (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    a's `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite`

-- "does not include any Television Receive-Only Satellite Receiving System": the television receiver is the apparatus used for the visual and aural reception, less any TVRO system.
GIVEN a IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the apparatus is a broadcast television receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    a's `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` AND (NOT (`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the apparatus is a TVRO system (RevEd 2004)` a))

GIVEN `the premises are registered under the Hotels Act (Cap. 127) for use as a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the premises are a hotel` MEANS
    `the premises are registered under the Hotels Act (Cap. 127) for use as a hotel`

-- src:162 | ‘‘vessel’’ includes any aircraft, ship or boat not propelled by oars.
@ref reg 2(1) "vessel" (src:162)
GIVEN `it is an aircraft, ship or boat not propelled by oars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the craft is a vessel` MEANS
    `it is an aircraft, ship or boat not propelled by oars`

-- src:163 | (2) Unless the context otherwise requires, the words ‘‘licence’’ and
-- src:164 | ‘‘licensee’’ shall, when used in or with reference to the following
-- src:165 | regulations, be construed respectively as meaning a licence or the
-- src:166 | person to whom is granted a licence of the type specified against
-- src:167 | such regulations, as the case may be:
-- src:168 | (a) regulations 17 to 22 — licence for dealing in broadcasting
-- src:169 | apparatus (other than a TVRO system);
-- src:170 | (b) regulations 23 to 26 — licence for broadcast sound receivers;
-- src:171 | (c) regulations 27 to 35 — licence for broadcast television
-- src:172 | receivers; and
-- src:173 | (d) regulations 36 and 37 — block licence for broadcast sound
-- src:174 | receivers and broadcast television receivers.
@ref reg 2(2): the type of licence each group of regulations is about (src:163-174)
GIVEN `the regulation number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 1 reg 2(2) the type of licence the regulation is about (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the regulation number` AT LEAST 17 AND `the regulation number` AT MOST 22 THEN JUST "licence for dealing in broadcasting apparatus (other than a TVRO system)"
           IF `the regulation number` AT LEAST 23 AND `the regulation number` AT MOST 26 THEN JUST "licence for broadcast sound receivers"
           IF `the regulation number` AT LEAST 27 AND `the regulation number` AT MOST 35 THEN JUST "licence for broadcast television receivers"
           IF `the regulation number` AT LEAST 36 AND `the regulation number` AT MOST 37 THEN JUST "block licence for broadcast sound receivers and broadcast television receivers"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 4: Operation of apparatus`

-- src:187 | Operation of apparatus
-- src:188 | 4.—(1) All apparatus for the reception of broadcast matter
-- src:189 | licensed under these Regulations shall be operated in such manner
-- src:190 | as to cause as little radiation as practicable from the aerial or from
-- src:191 | the apparatus itself, and shall not in any case exceed the values laid
-- src:192 | down in any regulations made under the Telecommunications Act
-- src:193 | (Cap. 323) governing interference from electrical apparatus.
-- src:194 | (2) Where any broadcasting apparatus is situated within 800
-- src:195 | metres of the boundary of any aerodrome, or within the approach
-- src:196 | funnel (as specified by the chief executive officer of the Civil Aviation
-- src:197 | Authority of Singapore) to any aerodrome, the aerial, or any mast
-- src:201 | supporting it, shall not exceed such height as may be approved by the
-- src:202 | chief executive officer of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore.
@ref reg 4(1) and (2) (src:187-202)
GIVEN `it is operated to cause as little radiation as practicable from the aerial or from the apparatus itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the radiation does not exceed the values laid down in any regulations made under the Telecommunications Act governing interference from electrical apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 4(1) the apparatus is operated as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `it is operated to cause as little radiation as practicable from the aerial or from the apparatus itself` AND `the radiation does not exceed the values laid down in any regulations made under the Telecommunications Act governing interference from electrical apparatus`

GIVEN `the apparatus is within 800 metres of the boundary of any aerodrome or within the approach funnel to any aerodrome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aerial or any mast supporting it does not exceed the height approved by the chief executive officer of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 4(2) the aerial or mast is as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the apparatus is within 800 metres of the boundary of any aerodrome or within the approach funnel to any aerodrome`) OR `the aerial or any mast supporting it does not exceed the height approved by the chief executive officer of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore`

-- src:203 | (3) Any aerial which crosses above or is liable to fall upon or to be
-- src:204 | blown on to any overhead telecommunication, power wire or power
-- src:205 | apparatus shall be adequately guarded.
@ref reg 4(3) (src:203-205)
GIVEN `the aerial crosses above or is liable to fall upon or be blown on to any overhead telecommunication, power wire or power apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is adequately guarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 4(3) the aerial is as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the aerial crosses above or is liable to fall upon or be blown on to any overhead telecommunication, power wire or power apparatus`) OR `it is adequately guarded`

§ `Regulation 5: Duration of and fee for licence`

-- src:624 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:625 | Regulation 5
-- src:627 | 1. Licence for dealing in broadcast sound receivers and $330 per annum.
-- src:628 | broadcast television receivers
-- src:629 | 2. Licence for a broadcast sound receiver $27 for 12 months.
-- src:630 | 3. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in $40 per annum.
-- src:631 | monochrome except as provided for in item 5
-- src:632 | 4. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in colour $110 per annum.
-- src:633 | except as provided for in item 6
-- src:634 | 29.2.2004
-- src:635 | Broadcasting (Television and Radio
-- src:636 | p. 16 2004 Ed.] Licensing) Regulations [CAP. 28, Rg 1
-- src:638 | FIRST SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:640 | 5. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in $30 per annum.
-- src:641 | monochrome installed in a hotel in which not less than
-- src:642 | 90% of the total number of rooms and suites have
-- src:643 | broadcast television receivers installed therein
-- src:644 | 6. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in colour $82.50 per annum.
-- src:645 | installed in a hotel in which not less than 90% of the
-- src:646 | total number of rooms and suites have broadcast
-- src:647 | television receivers installed therein
-- src:648 | 7. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in $20 per annum.
-- src:649 | monochrome installed in a hospital
-- src:650 | 8. Licence for a broadcast television receiver in colour $55 per annum.
-- src:651 | installed in a hospital
@ref First Schedule (fees) as printed in the Revised Edition 2004 (src:624-651)
-- First Schedule items: 1 $330 per annum; 2 $27 for 12 months; 3 $40; 4 $110; 5 $30; 6 $82.50; 7 $20; 8 $55.
GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 First Schedule the annual fee for the item` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the First Schedule` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 330
           IF ^ EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 27
           IF ^ EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 40
           IF ^ EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 110
           IF ^ EQUALS 5 THEN JUST 30
           IF ^ EQUALS 6 THEN JUST 82.5
           IF ^ EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 20
           IF ^ EQUALS 8 THEN JUST 55
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:207 | Duration of and fee for licence
-- src:208 | 5.—(1) The fee for any licence shall be payable in advance and
-- src:209 | shall be —
-- src:210 | (a) in the case of a licence for 12 months, the fee set out in the
-- src:211 | First Schedule; and
-- src:212 | (b) in the case of a licence for any other period, the pro-rata rate
-- src:213 | of the appropriate annual licence fee set out in the First
-- src:214 | Schedule.
-- src:215 | (2) Subject to regulation 37 (1), a licence (other than a licence for
-- src:216 | a broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle) shall be valid from
-- src:217 | the first day of the month in which it is issued, and remain valid for
-- src:218 | such period as the licensing authority may determine unless it is
-- src:219 | sooner determined in accordance with these Regulations.
-- src:220 | (3) A licence for a broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle
-- src:221 | shall, as from the date of its issue, be valid for such period as the
-- src:222 | licensing authority may determine unless it is sooner determined in
-- src:223 | accordance with these Regulations.
-- src:224 | (4) Where a licence has expired, it shall, subject to regulation 37 (1),
-- src:225 | be renewable for such period as the licensing authority may determine
-- src:226 | by the issue of a fresh licence commencing on the day following the
-- src:227 | date of expiry of the previous licence.
-- src:228 | (5) Any person in possession of a current broadcast sound receiver
-- src:229 | licence in respect of a vehicle or a vessel may, if the person so desires
-- src:230 | and upon payment of an additional fee, apply to have the licence
-- src:231 | varied to enable him to operate a broadcast television receiver until
-- src:232 | the date of the expiration of the licence.
-- src:233 | (6) The additional fee referred to in paragraph (5) would be the
-- src:234 | difference in the fee payable per annum for each unexpired year of
-- src:235 | the licence between a licence for a broadcast sound receiver and a
-- src:236 | licence for a broadcast television receiver as set out in the First
-- src:237 | Schedule, subject to a minimum of —
-- src:242 | (a) $13 in a case falling within item 3 of the First Schedule; or
-- src:243 | (b) $83 in a case falling within item 4 of the First Schedule.
-- src:244 | (7) Any person in possession of a current licence to operate a
-- src:245 | broadcast television receiver in monochrome may, upon payment of
-- src:246 | an additional fee, apply to have the licence varied to enable him to
-- src:247 | operate a broadcast television receiver in colour until the date of the
-- src:248 | expiration of the licence.
-- src:249 | (8) The additional fee referred to paragraph (7) would be the
-- src:250 | difference in the fee payable per annum for each unexpired year of
-- src:251 | the licence between a licence for a broadcast television receiver in
-- src:252 | monochrome and a licence for a broadcast television receiver in
-- src:253 | colour as set out in the First Schedule, subject to a minimum of —
-- src:254 | (a) $52.50 in a case falling within item 6 of the First Schedule;
-- src:255 | (b) $35 in a case falling within item 8 of the First Schedule; or
-- src:256 | (c) $70 in all other cases.
@ref reg 5 (RevEd 2004) (src:207-256)
-- reg 5(1): payable in advance; for 12 months the fee set out, for any other period the pro-rata rate of the annual fee. The text does not say in what unit a period is reckoned: whole months are asked.
GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months the licence is for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 5(1) the fee payable in advance for the licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Rg 1 First Schedule the annual fee for the item` `the item of the First Schedule`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST annual THEN JUST (IF `the number of months the licence is for` EQUALS 12 THEN annual ELSE annual TIMES `the number of months the licence is for` DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN `it is a licence for a broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the licence is issued` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the month in which the licence is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Rg 1 reg 5(2) and (3) the licence is valid from (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    IF `it is a licence for a broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle` THEN `the day the licence is issued` ELSE `the first day of the month in which the licence is issued`

GIVEN `the licence has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fresh licence commences on the day following the date of expiry of the previous licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 5(4) the licence is renewed as the regulation provides` MEANS
    `the licence has expired` AND `the fresh licence commences on the day following the date of expiry of the previous licence`

-- reg 5(5) and (6): variation of a sound receiver licence for a vehicle or a vessel into a television receiver licence. The additional fee is the difference in the annual fees for each unexpired year, subject to a minimum.
GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of unexpired years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 5(6) the additional fee for varying a sound receiver licence (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (IF (40 MINUS 27) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` GREATER THAN 13 THEN (40 MINUS 27) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` ELSE 13)
           IF ^ EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (IF (110 MINUS 27) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` GREATER THAN 83 THEN (110 MINUS 27) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` ELSE 83)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- reg 5(7) and (8): variation of a monochrome television licence into a colour licence.
GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of unexpired years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 5(8) the additional fee for varying a monochrome licence to a colour licence (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` EQUALS 6 THEN (IF (82.5 MINUS 30) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` GREATER THAN 52.5 THEN (82.5 MINUS 30) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` ELSE 52.5)
           IF ^ EQUALS 8 THEN (IF (55 MINUS 20) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` GREATER THAN 35 THEN (55 MINUS 20) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` ELSE 35)
           OTHERWISE (IF (110 MINUS 40) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` GREATER THAN 70 THEN (110 MINUS 40) TIMES `the number of unexpired years` ELSE 70)

§ `Regulation 6: Late payment fee`

-- src:258 | Late payment fee
-- src:259 | 6. A late payment fee for the grant or renewal of a licence for a
-- src:260 | broadcast sound receiver or a broadcast television receiver shall be
-- src:261 | in accordance with the Second Schedule.
-- src:654 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:655 | Regulation 6
-- src:657 | 1. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of a $10.
-- src:658 | broadcast sound receiver licence (if the application is
-- src:659 | made after 21 days following the expiration of the
-- src:660 | licence)
-- src:661 | 2. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of a $25.
-- src:662 | broadcast television receiver licence (if the application
-- src:663 | is made after 21 days following the expiration of the
-- src:664 | licence)
@ref reg 6 and the Second Schedule (RevEd 2004) (src:258-664)
-- Second Schedule as printed in this Edition: item 1, $10 for the grant or renewal of a broadcast sound receiver licence (if the application is made after 21 days following the expiration of the licence); item 2, $25 for a broadcast television receiver licence (same condition).
GIVEN `the licence is for a broadcast sound receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made after 21 days following the expiration of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 6 the late payment fee (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made after 21 days following the expiration of the licence` THEN (IF `the licence is for a broadcast sound receiver` THEN 10 ELSE 25) ELSE 0

§ `Regulation 7: Prosecution`

-- src:263 | Prosecution
-- src:264 | 7. In any prosecution against a person holding an expired licence
-- src:265 | in respect of a contravention of section 20 (1) of the Act or of
-- src:266 | regulation 17, 27 or 36 —
-- src:267 | (a) the subsequent renewal of the expired licence under
-- src:268 | regulation 5 (4) shall not in any way affect or prejudice such
-- src:269 | prosecution; and
-- src:270 | (b) unless the licensing authority has been notified in writing by
-- src:271 | that person that the broadcasting apparatus is no longer in
-- src:272 | his possession, the onus of proving the same shall lie upon
-- src:273 | that person.
@ref reg 7 (src:263-273)
GIVEN `the person holds an expired licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensing authority has been notified in writing by that person that the broadcasting apparatus is no longer in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 7(b) the onus of proving that the apparatus was no longer in the person's possession lies on the person (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person holds an expired licence` AND (NOT `the licensing authority has been notified in writing by that person that the broadcasting apparatus is no longer in the person's possession`)

GIVEN `the expired licence was subsequently renewed under regulation 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 7(a) the subsequent renewal affects or prejudices the prosecution` MEANS
    `the expired licence was subsequently renewed under regulation 5(4)` AND FALSE

§ `Regulation 8: Exemptions`

-- src:275 | Exemptions
-- src:276 | 8. The licensing authority may, in its discretion and subject to
-- src:277 | such conditions as it thinks fit, waive or reduce the payment of the
-- src:281 | fee payable for a licence for any broadcast sound receiver or any
-- src:282 | broadcast television receiver —
-- src:283 | (a) to a person who is required to use his broadcasting apparatus
-- src:284 | for Government purposes;
-- src:285 | (b) to a blind person for operating a broadcast sound receiver;
-- src:286 | (c) to a deaf person for operating a broadcast television
-- src:287 | receiver; or
-- src:288 | (d) in such other circumstances as may appear to the licensing
-- src:289 | authority to be reasonable.
@ref reg 8 (RevEd 2004) (src:275-289)
-- The licensing authority "may, in its discretion and subject to such conditions as it thinks fit, waive or reduce" the fee in these cases; the function says the case is within the discretion, not that the Authority will.
GIVEN `the person is required to use the person's broadcasting apparatus for Government purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is blind and the fee is for operating a broadcast sound receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deaf and the fee is for operating a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances appear to the licensing authority to be reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 8 the case is within the licensing authority's discretion to waive or reduce the fee (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person is required to use the person's broadcasting apparatus for Government purposes` OR `the person is blind and the fee is for operating a broadcast sound receiver` OR `the person is deaf and the fee is for operating a broadcast television receiver` OR `the circumstances appear to the licensing authority to be reasonable`

§ `Regulation 9: Termination of licence`

-- src:291 | Termination of licence
-- src:292 | 9.—(1) The licensing authority may, by notice in writing,
-- src:293 | determine any licence if the holder of the licence fails to comply with
-- src:294 | the Act or these Regulations or with any condition of the licence, and
-- src:295 | no fee or part thereof paid for such licence shall be refundable.
-- src:296 | (2) Where a licence is determined before its expiry for any reason
-- src:297 | other than those specified in paragraph (1), the licensing authority
-- src:298 | may, if it thinks fit, make a refund of the appropriate pro rata amount
-- src:299 | for the unexpired period of the licence.
@ref reg 9 (RevEd 2004) (src:291-299)
GIVEN `the holder fails to comply with the Act or these Regulations or with any condition of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 9(1) the licensing authority may by written notice determine the licence, and no fee is refundable (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the holder fails to comply with the Act or these Regulations or with any condition of the licence`

GIVEN `the licence is determined before its expiry for a reason other than failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 9(2) the licensing authority may make a pro rata refund for the unexpired period (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licence is determined before its expiry for a reason other than failure to comply`

§ `Regulation 10: Transfer, assignment or disposal of licence`

-- src:301 | Transfer, assignment or disposal of licence
-- src:302 | 10.—(1) Except as provided in paragraph (2), the holder of a
-- src:303 | licence shall not transfer, assign or otherwise dispose of the licence.
-- src:304 | (2) Where the registered owner of a vehicle transfers the
-- src:305 | registration of the vehicle to another person under the provisions of
-- src:306 | the Road Traffic Act (Cap. 276), any licence which may have been
-- src:307 | issued to him under these Regulations in respect of a broadcast sound
-- src:308 | receiver installed in the vehicle shall be deemed to have been
-- src:309 | transferred to the person to whom he has transferred the registration
-- src:310 | of the vehicle.
@ref reg 10 (src:301-310)
GIVEN `the registered owner transferred the registration of the vehicle to another person under the Road Traffic Act (Cap. 276)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is in respect of a broadcast sound receiver installed in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 10(2) the licence is deemed transferred to the person to whom the vehicle's registration was transferred` MEANS
    `the registered owner transferred the registration of the vehicle to another person under the Road Traffic Act (Cap. 276)` AND `the licence is in respect of a broadcast sound receiver installed in the vehicle`

GIVEN `the licence is deemed transferred under regulation 10(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 10(1) the holder may transfer, assign or otherwise dispose of the licence` MEANS
    `the licence is deemed transferred under regulation 10(2)`

§ `Regulation 11: Change of particulars`

-- src:312 | Change of particulars
-- src:313 | 11.—(1) The holder of a licence shall, subject to paragraph (2),
-- src:314 | notify the licensing authority of any change in his address or in any
-- src:315 | other of the particulars stated in the licence within 28 days of the
-- src:316 | change.
-- src:321 | (2) Where the holder of a licence who has changed his residential
-- src:322 | address makes a report of the change under section 8 of the National
-- src:323 | Registration Act (Cap. 201) within 28 days thereof, he shall be
-- src:324 | deemed to have notified the licensing authority of the change in his
-- src:325 | residential address in compliance with paragraph (1).
@ref reg 11 (RevEd 2004) (src:312-325)
GIVEN `the number of days from the change to the notification` IS A NUMBER
      `the holder changed the holder's residential address and made a report under section 8 of the National Registration Act (Cap. 201) within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 11 the holder has notified the licensing authority of the change in time (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the number of days from the change to the notification` AT MOST 28 OR `the holder changed the holder's residential address and made a report under section 8 of the National Registration Act (Cap. 201) within 28 days`

§ `Regulation 12: Telecommunications apparatus`

-- src:327 | Telecommunications apparatus
-- src:328 | 12.—(1) No broadcasting apparatus shall be used in a manner
-- src:329 | which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient
-- src:330 | working or maintenance of any telephone, telegraph or power line
-- src:331 | which already existed at the time the broadcasting apparatus was
-- src:332 | installed.
-- src:333 | (2) No person shall use any broadcasting apparatus in such manner
-- src:334 | as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by any
-- src:335 | other broadcasting apparatus licensed under these Regulations or
-- src:336 | the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323).
-- src:337 | (3) No unauthorised person shall intercept any sign, signal, writing,
-- src:338 | image, sound or intelligence of any nature transmitted by wire, radio,
-- src:339 | visual or other electromagnetic system, which is not intended for the
-- src:340 | general public.
@ref reg 12 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:327-340)
GIVEN `the broadcasting apparatus is used in a manner which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient working or maintenance of a telephone, telegraph or power line which already existed when the apparatus was installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(1) the use contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the broadcasting apparatus is used in a manner which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient working or maintenance of a telephone, telegraph or power line which already existed when the apparatus was installed`

GIVEN `the person uses broadcasting apparatus in such manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by other broadcasting apparatus licensed under these Regulations or the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(2) the use contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person uses broadcasting apparatus in such manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by other broadcasting apparatus licensed under these Regulations or the Telecommunications Act`

GIVEN `the person is unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intercepts a sign, signal, writing, image, sound or intelligence transmitted by wire, radio, visual or other electromagnetic system which is not intended for the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(3) the interception contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person is unauthorised` AND `the person intercepts a sign, signal, writing, image, sound or intelligence transmitted by wire, radio, visual or other electromagnetic system which is not intended for the general public`

§ `Regulations 13 to 15: Examination and information`

-- src:342 | Power to examine apparatus
-- src:343 | 13. Any officer authorised in that behalf by the licensing authority
-- src:344 | shall have power, on production of proof of identity, to enter at a
-- src:345 | reasonable hour any vehicle, vessel, aircraft, premises or other place
-- src:346 | where broadcasting apparatus is installed or is in the course of being
-- src:347 | installed to examine or test that broadcasting apparatus.
@ref reg 13 (RevEd 2004) (src:342-347)
GIVEN `the officer is authorised by the licensing authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer produces proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a reasonable hour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a vehicle, vessel, aircraft, premises or other place where broadcasting apparatus is installed or is in the course of being installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 13 the officer has power to enter and to examine or test the apparatus (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the officer is authorised by the licensing authority` AND `the officer produces proof of identity` AND `it is a reasonable hour` AND `the place is a vehicle, vessel, aircraft, premises or other place where broadcasting apparatus is installed or is in the course of being installed`

-- src:349 | Power to examine licence
-- src:350 | 14. Any officer authorised in that behalf by the licensing authority
-- src:351 | or any police officer shall be entitled, on production of proof of
-- src:352 | identity, to examine any licence issued under the Act or these
-- src:353 | Regulations.
@ref reg 14 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:349-353)
GIVEN `the person is an officer authorised by the licensing authority or a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person produces proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 14 the person is entitled to examine any licence issued under the Act or these Regulations (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person is an officer authorised by the licensing authority or a police officer` AND `the person produces proof of identity`

-- src:355 | Information
-- src:356 | 15. The licensing authority may, by notice in writing, require any
-- src:357 | person to furnish within a reasonable time such information as may
-- src:361 | be considered necessary, being information within the possession of
-- src:362 | that person, for the purposes of the Act or these Regulations.
@ref reg 15 (RevEd 2004) (src:355-362)
GIVEN `the licensing authority has required the person by notice in writing to furnish information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is considered necessary for the purposes of the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is within the possession of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 15 the person must furnish the information within a reasonable time (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licensing authority has required the person by notice in writing to furnish information` AND `the information is considered necessary for the purposes of the Act or these Regulations` AND `the information is within the possession of that person`

§ `Part III: Dealers in broadcasting apparatus (regulations 16 to 22)`

-- src:364 | PART III
-- src:365 | DEALERS IN
-- src:366 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:368 | Broadcasting system not to include TVRO system
-- src:369 | 16. In this Part, a reference to any broadcasting apparatus shall not
-- src:370 | include a reference to any TVRO system or part thereof.
@ref reg 16 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004), with the heading of Part III (src:364-370)
GIVEN `the apparatus is a TVRO system or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 16 the apparatus is broadcasting apparatus for the purposes of this Part (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    NOT `the apparatus is a TVRO system or part of one`

-- src:372 | Dealers in apparatus
-- src:373 | 17.—(1) No person shall offer for sale, sell or have in his
-- src:374 | possession with a view to sale in the course of his business any
-- src:375 | broadcasting apparatus without a licence to deal in such apparatus
-- src:376 | and in respect of such place of business.
-- src:377 | (2) A person to whom a licence is granted shall, in respect of all
-- src:378 | broadcasting apparatus sold by him, keep at every place of his
-- src:379 | business a register in such form as the licensing authority may require.
-- src:380 | (3) For the purposes of this regulation, ‘‘sale’’, with its grammatical
-- src:381 | variations, includes all transactions whatsoever as the result of which
-- src:382 | the ownership of or an interest in goods is or may be transferred or
-- src:383 | created.
-- src:384 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation, any sale made by a
-- src:385 | travelling salesman in the employ of a licensee shall be deemed to
-- src:386 | have been made at the premises specified in the licence of that
-- src:387 | licensee.
@ref reg 17 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:372-387)
GIVEN `the person offers for sale, sells or has in possession with a view to sale in the course of business any broadcasting apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a licence to deal in such apparatus and in respect of that place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 17(1) the person contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person offers for sale, sells or has in possession with a view to sale in the course of business any broadcasting apparatus` AND (NOT `the person has a licence to deal in such apparatus and in respect of that place of business`)

GIVEN `the person is a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person keeps at every place of business a register of all broadcasting apparatus sold, in the form the licensing authority may require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 17(2) the licensee keeps the register as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the person is a licensee`) OR `the person keeps at every place of business a register of all broadcasting apparatus sold, in the form the licensing authority may require`

GIVEN `the sale was made by a travelling salesman in the employ of a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 17(4) the sale is deemed made at the premises specified in the licence of that licensee (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the sale was made by a travelling salesman in the employ of a licensee`

-- src:389 | Application for dealers’ licence
-- src:390 | 18. An application for a dealer’s licence shall be made to the
-- src:391 | licensing authority in writing.
@ref reg 18 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:389-391)
GIVEN `the application for a dealer's licence is made to the licensing authority in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 18 the application is as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the application for a dealer's licence is made to the licensing authority in writing`

-- src:393 | Demonstration of apparatus
-- src:394 | 19.—(1) The possession of a licence shall entitle the licensee to
-- src:395 | demonstrate broadcasting apparatus at his place of business and at
-- src:402 | the premises of prospective customers, but shall not entitle him to
-- src:403 | operate the apparatus for the transmission of broadcast matter or
-- src:404 | radiocommunication apparatus for demonstration.
-- src:405 | (2) In this regulation, ‘‘radiocommunication apparatus’’ means
-- src:406 | any apparatus capable of transmitting radio waves.
@ref reg 19 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:393-406)
GIVEN `the licensee operates the apparatus for the transmission of broadcast matter or radiocommunication apparatus for demonstration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 19(1) the licence entitles the licensee to demonstrate the apparatus in that way (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    NOT `the licensee operates the apparatus for the transmission of broadcast matter or radiocommunication apparatus for demonstration`

-- src:408 | Exhibition of licence
-- src:409 | 20. The licensee shall exhibit his licence conspicuously in his place
-- src:410 | of business.
@ref reg 20 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:408-410)
GIVEN `the licensee exhibits the licence conspicuously in the place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 20 the licensee complies (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licensee exhibits the licence conspicuously in the place of business`

-- src:412 | Purchaser to furnish particulars
-- src:413 | 21. Every purchaser of broadcasting apparatus from a licensee
-- src:414 | shall furnish his name and address to the licensee.
@ref reg 21 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:412-414)
GIVEN `the purchaser furnishes name and address to the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 21 the purchaser complies (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the purchaser furnishes name and address to the licensee`

-- src:416 | Inspection of register
-- src:417 | 22.—(1) A licensee shall at all reasonable times permit any officer
-- src:418 | authorised in that behalf by the licensing authority to inspect the
-- src:419 | register kept in accordance with regulation 17 (2).
-- src:420 | (2) The licensee shall —
-- src:421 | (a) supply copies of entries in that register or make a nil return
-- src:422 | at the end of every calendar month to the licensing authority
-- src:423 | or to any other officer whom the licensing authority may
-- src:424 | direct; and
-- src:425 | (b) furnish to the licensing authority or such officer such
-- src:426 | information as may be required with reference to sales of
-- src:427 | broadcasting apparatus.
-- src:428 | (3) Every such register shall be preserved by the licensee so that at
-- src:429 | any time full particulars of transactions in the preceding calendar year
-- src:430 | are available for inspection.
-- src:431 | (4) Dealers shall notify every purchaser of a broadcasting apparatus
-- src:432 | of the obligation to obtain a licence for the operation of the set in
-- src:433 | Singapore.
@ref reg 22 (RevEd 2004; deleted by S 333/2004) (src:416-433)
GIVEN `the licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect the register at all reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee supplies copies of entries or makes a nil return at the end of every calendar month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee furnishes the information required about sales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is preserved so that full particulars of transactions in the preceding calendar year are available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 22(1) to (3) the licensee complies (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect the register at all reasonable times` AND `the licensee supplies copies of entries or makes a nil return at the end of every calendar month` AND `the licensee furnishes the information required about sales` AND `the register is preserved so that full particulars of transactions in the preceding calendar year are available`

GIVEN `the dealer notifies every purchaser of broadcasting apparatus of the obligation to obtain a licence for the operation of the set in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 22(4) the dealer complies (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the dealer notifies every purchaser of broadcasting apparatus of the obligation to obtain a licence for the operation of the set in Singapore`

§ `Part IV: Broadcast sound receivers (regulations 23 to 26)`

-- src:437 | PART IV
-- src:438 | BROADCAST SOUND RECEIVERS
-- src:440 | Broadcast sound receivers for vehicles or vessels
-- src:441 | 23.—(1) A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound
-- src:442 | receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship
-- src:443 | station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications
-- src:444 | Act (Cap. 323).
-- src:445 | (2) An application for a licence may be made at any post office or
-- src:446 | at such other places as the licensing authority may require.
-- src:447 | (3) A licence in respect of a broadcast sound receiver installed on
-- src:448 | board a vessel shall be granted only in the name of the owner or
-- src:449 | charterer of the vessel.
-- src:450 | (4) A licence issued in a place other than Singapore for any
-- src:451 | broadcast sound receiver shall permit the use of the receiver in
-- src:452 | Singapore for a period not exceeding 2 months.
-- src:453 | (5) For the purposes of this regulation, a broadcast sound receiver,
-- src:454 | other than one which is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel, shall be
-- src:455 | deemed to be installed therein if it is affixed in that vehicle or vessel
-- src:456 | by means of brackets or other mountings whether temporarily or
-- src:457 | permanently.
@ref reg 23 (RevEd 2004), with the heading of Part IV (src:437-457)
-- (1): a licence "shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted". A ship station licence can be granted only for a vessel, so the last limb is read as qualifying "vessel" (reading note R-3 in NOTES.md; no outcome differs).
-- (5): "other than one which is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel" is deemed installed if affixed by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently.
GIVEN `the receiver is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(5) the broadcast sound receiver is deemed installed (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the receiver is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel`) AND `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently`

GIVEN `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is installed in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(1) a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` OR (`the receiver is installed in a vessel` AND (NOT `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`))

GIVEN `the licence was issued in a place other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months the receiver is used in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(4) the licence permits the use of the broadcast sound receiver in Singapore (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licence was issued in a place other than Singapore` AND `the number of months the receiver is used in Singapore` AT MOST 2

GIVEN `the person applying is the owner or charterer of the vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(3) the licence for a receiver on board a vessel may be granted to the person (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person applying is the owner or charterer of the vessel`

-- src:459 | Exemption for temporary use of broadcast sound receiver
-- src:460 | 24. A licence shall not be required for the temporary use of a
-- src:461 | broadcast sound receiver in a public place or at an official or social
-- src:462 | function or a function organised for charitable purposes.
@ref reg 24 (src:459-462)
GIVEN `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 24 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a broadcast sound receiver` MEANS
    `the use is temporary` AND `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`

-- src:464 | Dimensions of external aerial
-- src:465 | 25. The combined height and length of an external aerial for a
-- src:466 | fixed broadcast sound receiver shall not, except with the written
-- src:467 | consent of the licensing authority, exceed 30 metres.
@ref reg 25 (RevEd 2004) (src:464-467)
GIVEN `the combined height and length of the external aerial of the fixed receiver in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `the licensing authority gave written consent to exceed 30 metres` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 25 the external aerial is as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the combined height and length of the external aerial of the fixed receiver in metres` AT MOST 30 OR `the licensing authority gave written consent to exceed 30 metres`

-- src:469 | Licensee may be required to cease operating broadcast sound receiver
-- src:470 | 26. A licensee shall, if so required by the licensing authority, cease
-- src:471 | to operate a broadcast sound receiver for any period specified by the
-- src:472 | licensing authority.
@ref reg 26 (RevEd 2004) (src:469-472)
GIVEN `the licensing authority requires the licensee to cease to operate the receiver for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 26 the licensee must cease to operate the broadcast sound receiver for that period (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licensing authority requires the licensee to cease to operate the receiver for a period`

§ `Part V: Broadcast television receivers (regulations 27 to 35)`

-- src:477 | PART V
-- src:478 | BROADCAST TELEVISION RECEIVERS
-- src:480 | Licence for broadcast television receiver
-- src:481 | 27.—(1) No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver
-- src:482 | without a licence.
-- src:483 | (2) An application for a licence may be made at any post office or
-- src:484 | at such other places as the licensing authority may require.
-- src:485 | (3) A licence shall permit the use of one or more broadcast
-- src:486 | television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the
-- src:487 | licensee, members of his family and domestic servants resident at the
-- src:488 | address specified therein.
-- src:489 | (4) A separate licence shall be required for a broadcast television
-- src:490 | receiver used by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or any person
-- src:491 | occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy,
-- src:492 | irrespective of whether or not such broadcast television receivers are
-- src:493 | connected to a common aerial, wire or cable.
@ref reg 27 (RevEd 2004), with the heading of Part V (src:477-493)
GIVEN `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` AND (NOT `the person has a licence`)

-- (3): a licence permits one or more television receivers and one or more sound receivers by the licensee, members of the family and domestic servants resident at the address specified in it.
GIVEN `the user is the licensee, a member of the licensee's family or a domestic servant resident at the address specified in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(3) the licence permits the use of the television receivers and sound receivers by the user (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the user is the licensee, a member of the licensee's family or a domestic servant resident at the address specified in the licence`

GIVEN `the receiver is used by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or a person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(4) a separate licence is required (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is used by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or a person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy`

-- src:495 | Broadcast television receiver in vehicle or vessel
-- src:496 | 28.—(1) If any person wishes to mount a broadcast television
-- src:497 | receiver in a vehicle or vessel, the owner of the vehicle or vessel shall
-- src:498 | ensure that the receiver is so mounted that it is not possible for the
-- src:499 | viewing screen to be seen from the normal driving position or from
-- src:500 | the helmsman’s position.
-- src:501 | (2) A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast
-- src:502 | television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect
-- src:503 | of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the
-- src:504 | Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323).
-- src:505 | (3) A licence in respect of a broadcast television receiver installed
-- src:506 | on board a vessel shall be granted only in the name of the owner or
-- src:507 | charterer of the vessel.
-- src:508 | (4) A licence issued in a place other than Singapore for any
-- src:509 | broadcast television receiver shall permit the use of the receiver in
-- src:510 | Singapore for a period not exceeding 2 months.
-- src:511 | (5) For the purposes of this regulation, a broadcast television
-- src:512 | receiver, other than one which is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel,
-- src:516 | shall be deemed to be installed therein if it is affixed in that vehicle
-- src:517 | or vessel by means of brackets or other mountings whether
-- src:518 | temporarily or permanently.
@ref reg 28 (RevEd 2004) (src:495-518)
GIVEN `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is installed in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` OR (`the receiver is installed in a vessel` AND (NOT `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`))

GIVEN `the viewing screen can be seen from the normal driving position or from the helmsman's position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(1) the owner has mounted the receiver as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    NOT `the viewing screen can be seen from the normal driving position or from the helmsman's position`

GIVEN `the receiver is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(5) the broadcast television receiver is deemed installed (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the receiver is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel`) AND `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently`

-- src:520 | Exemption for temporary use of broadcast television receiver
-- src:521 | 29. A licence shall not be required for the temporary use of a
-- src:522 | broadcast television receiver in a public place or at an official or social
-- src:523 | function or a function organised for charitable purposes.
@ref reg 29 (src:520-523)
GIVEN `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 29 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a broadcast television receiver` MEANS
    `the use is temporary` AND `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`

-- src:525 | Broadcast television receivers in schools or institutions
-- src:526 | 30.—(1) Subject to paragraph (2), in the case of a school or such
-- src:527 | other institution as the licensing authority may for the purposes of
-- src:528 | this regulation approve, a licence shall be regarded as permitting the
-- src:529 | use therein of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or
-- src:530 | more broadcast sound receivers.
-- src:531 | (2) A separate licence shall be required in respect of any broadcast
-- src:532 | television receiver used by any member of the staff in residential
-- src:533 | quarters, whether or not the quarters form part of the main premises
-- src:534 | of the school or institution referred to in paragraph (1).
@ref reg 30 (RevEd 2004) (src:525-534)
GIVEN `the premises are those of a school or an institution the licensing authority has approved for this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 30(2) a separate licence is required for the receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the premises are those of a school or an institution the licensing authority has approved for this regulation` AND `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters`

GIVEN `the premises are those of a school or an institution the licensing authority has approved for this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 30(1) the licence is regarded as permitting the use in the premises of television receivers and sound receivers (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the premises are those of a school or an institution the licensing authority has approved for this regulation` AND (NOT `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters`)

-- src:536 | Broadcast television receivers in hospitals
-- src:537 | 31.—(1) A separate licence shall be required —
-- src:538 | (a) for every broadcast television receiver installed in a hospital
-- src:539 | and for every extension from that broadcast television
-- src:540 | receiver; and
-- src:541 | (b) in respect of every broadcast television receiver used by a
-- src:542 | member of the staff in residential quarters, whether or not
-- src:543 | the quarters form part of the main premises.
-- src:544 | (2) A licence under paragraph (1) (a) shall permit the use of one or
-- src:545 | more broadcast sound receivers.
@ref reg 31 (RevEd 2004) (src:536-545)
GIVEN `the receiver is installed in a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is an extension from a receiver installed in a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 31(1) a separate licence is required for the receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed in a hospital` OR `the receiver is an extension from a receiver installed in a hospital` OR `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters`

GIVEN `the licence is under regulation 31(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 31(2) the licence permits the use of one or more broadcast sound receivers (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licence is under regulation 31(1)(a)`

-- src:547 | Broadcast television receivers in hotels
-- src:548 | 32.—(1) A licence taken out by the proprietor of a hotel shall be
-- src:549 | regarded as permitting the use therein of one or more broadcast
-- src:550 | television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the
-- src:551 | proprietor, members of his family and resident staff, or by any person
-- src:552 | in any common room at the disposal of paying guests.
-- src:557 | (2) A separate licence shall be required in respect of any broadcast
-- src:558 | television receiver used in each and every apartment of any paying
-- src:559 | guest in a hotel.
-- src:560 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2), any extension from a
-- src:561 | broadcast television receiver shall require a separate licence.
@ref reg 32 (RevEd 2004) (src:547-561)
GIVEN `the user is the proprietor of a hotel, a member of the proprietor's family, resident staff, or a person in a common room at the disposal of paying guests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 32(1) the hotel proprietor's licence is regarded as permitting the use (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the user is the proprietor of a hotel, a member of the proprietor's family, resident staff, or a person in a common room at the disposal of paying guests`

GIVEN `the receiver is used in an apartment of a paying guest in a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is an extension from a receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 32(2) and (3) a separate licence is required for the receiver (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is used in an apartment of a paying guest in a hotel` OR (`the receiver is an extension from a receiver` AND `the receiver is used in an apartment of a paying guest in a hotel`)

-- src:563 | Restricted monochrome licence
-- src:564 | 33. For the purposes of regulations 27, 30 and 32, a licence to
-- src:565 | operate a broadcast television receiver in monochrome shall not be
-- src:566 | regarded as permitting the use of any broadcast television receiver in
-- src:567 | colour.
@ref reg 33 (RevEd 2004) (src:563-567)
GIVEN `the licence is to operate a broadcast television receiver in monochrome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is used in colour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 33 the licence is regarded as permitting the use (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    NOT (`the licence is to operate a broadcast television receiver in monochrome` AND `the receiver is used in colour`)

-- src:569 | Dimensions of broadcast television receivers aerials
-- src:570 | 34. The licensing authority may, in its discretion, require that the
-- src:571 | aerial for any broadcast television receiver shall comply with the
-- src:572 | authority’s specifications with regard to dimensions, height and
-- src:573 | method of support.
@ref reg 34 (RevEd 2004) (src:569-573)
GIVEN `the licensing authority requires the aerial to comply with its specifications as to dimensions, height and method of support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aerial complies with those specifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 34 the aerial is as the licensing authority requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensing authority requires the aerial to comply with its specifications as to dimensions, height and method of support`) OR `the aerial complies with those specifications`

-- src:575 | Licensee may be required to cease operating broadcast television
-- src:576 | receiver
-- src:577 | 35. A licensee shall, if so required by the licensing authority, cease
-- src:578 | to operate a broadcast television receiver for any period specified by
-- src:579 | the licensing authority.
@ref reg 35 (RevEd 2004) (src:575-579)
GIVEN `the licensing authority requires the licensee to cease to operate the receiver for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 35 the licensee must cease to operate the broadcast television receiver for that period (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licensing authority requires the licensee to cease to operate the receiver for a period`

§ `Part VI: Block licence (regulations 36 and 37)`

-- src:581 | PART VI
-- src:582 | BLOCK LICENCE FOR
-- src:583 | BROADCAST SOUND RECEIVERS AND
-- src:584 | BROADCAST TELEVISION RECEIVERS
-- src:585 | IN HOTELS AND HOSPITALS
-- src:587 | Block licence
-- src:588 | 36. Notwithstanding the provisions of Parts IV and V, in the case
-- src:589 | of a hotel or hospital, the licensing authority may permit the owner of
-- src:590 | the hotel or hospital to apply for a block licence for all the broadcast
-- src:591 | television receivers installed in the hotel or hospital, as the case may
-- src:592 | be.
@ref reg 36 (RevEd 2004), with the heading of Part VI (src:581-592)
GIVEN `the person owns a hotel or hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensing authority permits the owner to apply for a block licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 36 the owner may apply for a block licence for all the broadcast television receivers installed in the hotel or hospital (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the person owns a hotel or hospital` AND `the licensing authority permits the owner to apply for a block licence`

-- src:596 | Licensing authority empowered to vary expiration dates
-- src:597 | 37.—(1) Where the existing licences for the broadcast television
-- src:598 | receivers in any hotel or hospital have different expiry dates, the
-- src:599 | licensing authority shall be empowered to vary the different expiry
-- src:600 | dates of those licences to one common expiry date in issuing a block
-- src:601 | licence.
-- src:602 | (2) The licensing authority, in varying the different expiry dates
-- src:603 | of the licences under paragraph (1), shall take into account any
-- src:604 | unexpired portion of the period of the licences and make appropriate
-- src:605 | adjustments to the amount of licence fees payable for the block
-- src:606 | licence.
@ref reg 37 (RevEd 2004) (src:596-606)
GIVEN `the licences of the receivers in a hotel or hospital have different expiry dates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 37(1) the licensing authority may vary the expiry dates to one common expiry date in issuing a block licence (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the licences of the receivers in a hotel or hospital have different expiry dates`

GIVEN `the unexpired portion of the licences was taken into account and the licence fees for the block licence were adjusted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 37(2) the licensing authority has acted as the regulation requires (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `the unexpired portion of the licences was taken into account and the licence fees for the block licence were adjusted`

§ `Part VII: Miscellaneous (regulations 38 and 39)`

-- src:608 | PART VII
-- src:609 | MISCELLANEOUS
-- src:615 | Authority not liable
-- src:616 | 39.—(1) Nothing in these Regulations shall be construed as
-- src:617 | rendering the Authority liable or responsible for any infringement by
-- src:618 | a licensee in the exercise of his licence of copyright in any work or
-- src:619 | of any patent for an invention or for any breach of any written law
-- src:620 | arising out of the exercise of the licence.
-- src:621 | (2) Nothing in these Regulations shall affect the liability of the
-- src:622 | licensee in respect of any such act done by him.
@ref reg 39, with the heading of Part VII (src:608-622)
GIVEN `the infringement is of copyright or of a patent, or a breach of written law arising from the exercise of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 39 the Authority is liable or responsible for the infringement or breach` MEANS
    `the infringement is of copyright or of a patent, or a breach of written law arising from the exercise of the licence` AND FALSE
